255
00:14:59,858 --> 00:15:04,697
And then we can talk
about Michael all you want.

256
00:15:13,581 --> 00:15:15,165
Got something!

257
00:15:16,500 --> 00:15:18,586
Ah!

258
00:15:28,470 --> 00:15:30,431
Nope.

259
00:15:30,514 --> 00:15:32,349
Not hers.

260
00:15:32,433 --> 00:15:33,976
It's got a totally
different vibration.

261
00:15:34,059 --> 00:15:37,104
Moira's bones would be
much more morose.

262
00:15:37,187 --> 00:15:39,356
You know this
is ridiculous, right?

263
00:15:39,440 --> 00:15:40,774
This place has more bodies buried

264
00:15:40,858 --> 00:15:42,484
than the catacombs in Rome.

265
00:15:42,568 --> 00:15:45,029
If Constance wants us
to get rid of the maid,

266
00:15:45,112 --> 00:15:48,157
I know a spell that can
easily bind her to the closet.

267
00:15:48,240 --> 00:15:49,658
She'll never have
to see her again.

268
00:15:49,742 --> 00:15:51,410
Keep digging.

269
00:15:52,494 --> 00:15:54,038
Ah!

270
00:16:05,924 --> 00:16:07,051
You have an enemy.

271
00:16:07,134 --> 00:16:11,472
I'm proud to say I have many.

272
00:16:11,555 --> 00:16:13,307
You can't live with virtue

273
00:16:13,390 --> 00:16:15,934
without getting on the bad side
of those without.

274
00:16:16,018 --> 00:16:18,604
Constance hates your guts.

275
00:16:18,687 --> 00:16:21,023
She won't talk to us
unless we put you away.

276
00:16:21,106 --> 00:16:25,736
Out of sight forever.

277
00:16:25,819 --> 00:16:28,280
What are you going to do to me?

278
00:16:33,160 --> 00:16:36,830
<i>(Gasps)</i>
Oh, heavens be.

279
00:16:36,914 --> 00:16:38,916
My bones.

280
00:16:40,959 --> 00:16:43,087
I can't begin to thank you.

281
00:16:43,170 --> 00:16:45,714
These bones are my means
to escape.

282
00:16:45,798 --> 00:16:49,468
Oh, thank you, thank you,
thank you.

283
00:16:49,551 --> 00:16:53,138
<i>(Whispering)</i> Thank you. Thank you.

284
00:16:53,222 --> 00:16:55,224
Okay.

285
00:16:56,642 --> 00:17:00,312
Okay, you're getting slobber
on my clothes.

286
00:17:00,396 --> 00:17:03,315
- <i>(Sniffs, clears throat)</i>
- Moira.

287
00:17:03,399 --> 00:17:06,026
You have a choice.

288
00:17:06,110 --> 00:17:08,612
Where do you want to be buried?

289
00:17:10,656 --> 00:17:15,452
There's only one place
I've ever wanted to be.

290
00:17:21,375 --> 00:17:23,127
How original,

291
00:17:23,210 --> 00:17:24,962
to be buried in a cemetery.

292
00:17:25,045 --> 00:17:28,507
Her wish was to be close
to her mother.

293
00:17:28,590 --> 00:17:31,468
I want my bones to be buried
at the studio.

294
00:17:31,552 --> 00:17:33,637
Paramount, Stage 7.

295
00:17:33,721 --> 00:17:37,891
I would gladly haunt the shit
out of that place.

296
00:17:37,975 --> 00:17:40,686
It's where they made me do
my first nude scene.

297
00:17:40,769 --> 00:17:42,980
Totally gratuitous.

298
00:17:43,063 --> 00:17:45,607
I begged for a body double,

299
00:17:45,691 --> 00:17:48,652
but the asshole producer wanted
to get his rocks off, so...

300
00:17:48,736 --> 00:17:50,446
You surprised me.

301
00:17:50,529 --> 00:17:53,365
Under the facade
of a heartless narcissist...

302
00:17:53,449 --> 00:17:54,700
Is a stone-cold bitch.

303
00:17:54,783 --> 00:17:56,994
Listen, warlock,

304
00:17:57,077 --> 00:17:58,722
I wouldn't think twice
about slitting your throat

305
00:17:58,746 --> 00:18:00,515
if I thought it would get me
out of that house

306
00:18:00,539 --> 00:18:01,819
a second sooner with the answers.

307
00:18:01,874 --> 00:18:04,251
Duly warned.

308
00:18:07,254 --> 00:18:09,631
<i>(Both sigh)</i>

310
00:18:41,205 --> 00:18:44,124
Oh, Mother.

311
00:18:46,293 --> 00:18:49,797
Your hands.

312
00:18:52,591 --> 00:18:54,593
They're as beautiful
as I remembered.

313
00:18:58,388 --> 00:18:59,848
What's wrong?

314
00:19:01,725 --> 00:19:05,354
I have to confess something.

315
00:19:05,437 --> 00:19:07,064
I killed you.

316
00:19:09,441 --> 00:19:12,611
I pulled the plug on the respirator

317
00:19:12,694 --> 00:19:14,613
because I couldn't bear leaving you

318
00:19:14,696 --> 00:19:16,448
in that horrible nursing home.

319
00:19:18,534 --> 00:19:19,993
Can you ever forgive me?

320
00:19:20,077 --> 00:19:22,454
Darling,

321
00:19:22,538 --> 00:19:26,708
I wanted to smother you with kisses.

322
00:19:26,792 --> 00:19:31,046
I was in agony,
and you gave me peace.

323
00:19:32,089 --> 00:19:34,341
- Oh.
- Oh.

324
00:19:38,053 --> 00:19:39,221
It's beautiful here.

325
00:19:41,056 --> 00:19:43,392
I feel like I can finally breathe.

327
00:20:26,435 --> 00:20:27,769
MADISON: We did what you asked.

328
00:20:27,853 --> 00:20:29,104
Moira's gone,

329
00:20:29,187 --> 00:20:32,065
- so you can start any time now.
- Shh...

330
00:20:33,817 --> 00:20:38,280
I was just savoring
the stillness.

331
00:20:38,363 --> 00:20:40,407
Not only was that woman

332
00:20:40,490 --> 00:20:43,827
the worst maid in God's creation,

333
00:20:43,911 --> 00:20:45,829
but she would never shut up.

334
00:20:45,913 --> 00:20:48,665
Death only made her more verbose.

335
00:20:48,749 --> 00:20:50,584
Tell us about Michael.

336
00:20:50,667 --> 00:20:54,713
Well...

337
00:20:54,796 --> 00:20:57,132
he was born right here
in this house

338
00:20:57,215 --> 00:20:59,885
to a mother and a family

339
00:20:59,968 --> 00:21:02,846
ultimately marked for death.

340
00:21:02,930 --> 00:21:04,848
<i>(Screams)</i>

342
00:21:11,480 --> 00:21:12,814
<i>When his mother died</i>

343
00:21:12,898 --> 00:21:15,359
<i>pushing him out into the world,</i>

344
00:21:15,442 --> 00:21:17,986
<i>I gladly assumed the burden</i>

345
00:21:18,070 --> 00:21:20,572
<i>of raising him.</i>

346
00:21:20,656 --> 00:21:23,825
You see, I-I-I am a mother myself,

347
00:21:23,909 --> 00:21:26,536
four times over.

348
00:21:26,620 --> 00:21:28,622
- <i>(Chuckles)</i>
- Why you?

349
00:21:28,705 --> 00:21:29,873
Because

350
00:21:29,957 --> 00:21:31,708
he also happened to be my grandson.

351
00:21:31,792 --> 00:21:34,795
His father was that handsome

352
00:21:34,878 --> 00:21:38,048
young man in the sweater
and the mop top

353
00:21:38,131 --> 00:21:41,343
that you saw when you
first came in... Tate.

354
00:21:41,426 --> 00:21:44,763
Now, I am the first
to admit that, um,

355
00:21:44,846 --> 00:21:48,767
there were mistakes made raising Tate.

356
00:21:48,850 --> 00:21:52,187
<i>And that's why, with Michael...
oh, my God...</i>

357
00:21:52,270 --> 00:21:54,523
<i>he was such a perfect</i>

358
00:21:54,606 --> 00:21:57,234
<i>little angel of light.</i>

359
00:21:57,317 --> 00:22:00,946
<i>I thought that would be
my chance for a do-over.</i>

360
00:22:01,029 --> 00:22:04,783
You see, I was born to be a mother.

361
00:22:04,866 --> 00:22:07,077
I always felt that,

362
00:22:07,160 --> 00:22:10,580
<i>to raise a great man,</i>

363
00:22:10,664 --> 00:22:15,419
<i>that was the most admirable
and selfless act</i>

364
00:22:15,502 --> 00:22:17,838
<i>a woman could aspire to.</i>

365
00:22:17,921 --> 00:22:20,382
<i>He was my destiny.</i>

366
00:22:20,465 --> 00:22:22,467
<i>Oh, such a beautiful child,</i>

367
00:22:22,551 --> 00:22:25,721
<i>with such a cheerful disposition.</i>

368
00:22:25,804 --> 00:22:30,684
Even when he was committing
unspeakable acts.

369
00:22:30,767 --> 00:22:32,144
What do you mean unspeakable?

370
00:22:32,227 --> 00:22:36,189
Well, it was trivial at first,
of course, you know.

371
00:22:36,273 --> 00:22:37,691
I'd find dead flies in his crib

372
00:22:37,774 --> 00:22:40,569
with their wings shorn off and...

373
00:22:40,652 --> 00:22:45,657
And then, as he got older...
small rodents.

374
00:22:45,741 --> 00:22:48,577
I had seen enough

375
00:22:48,660 --> 00:22:51,747
Discovery Channel specials
to know exactly

376
00:22:51,830 --> 00:22:54,624
what evolutionary tree
he was shimmying up.

377
00:22:54,708 --> 00:22:57,044
Bundy, Dahmer,

378
00:22:57,127 --> 00:23:00,922
they started
with small animals, too...

379
00:23:01,006 --> 00:23:04,676
until they graduated

380
00:23:04,760 --> 00:23:06,762
to grander things.

381
00:23:10,640 --> 00:23:15,979
<i>He said they were presents
because he loved me.</i>

382
00:23:16,063 --> 00:23:18,315
<i>Oh, and his love did flow.</i>

383
00:23:18,398 --> 00:23:20,525
<i>And enjoyable as it was,
to have a child</i>

384
00:23:20,609 --> 00:23:24,279
so committed to expressing
his love for me,

385
00:23:24,362 --> 00:23:27,199
<i>I did try to encourage him
to find</i>

386
00:23:27,282 --> 00:23:29,993
<i>another avenue of expression.</i>

387
00:23:30,077 --> 00:23:31,745
<i>Still, nothing I could say</i>

388
00:23:31,828 --> 00:23:34,581
<i>would get him to cease.</i>

389
00:23:34,664 --> 00:23:37,501
<i>Each time I would dutifully</i>

390
00:23:37,584 --> 00:23:42,297
<i>bury one of these gifts along
with a little piece of my soul.</i>

391
00:23:42,380 --> 00:23:45,634
<i>Well, I tried to find</i>

392
00:23:45,717 --> 00:23:48,345
<i>a silver lining</i>

393
00:23:48,428 --> 00:23:50,305
<i>to make lemonade out of lemons,</i>

394
00:23:50,388 --> 00:23:53,683
<i>so every time I buried
one of his presents,</i>

395
00:23:53,767 --> 00:23:55,560
<i>I planted a rose bush on top.</i>

396
00:23:55,644 --> 00:23:58,188
You know, from death

397
00:23:58,271 --> 00:24:00,732
springs life eternal.

398
00:24:02,275 --> 00:24:05,362
You are childless, I presume?

399
00:24:05,445 --> 00:24:08,907
A skinny little thing like you
would struggle to carry.

400
00:24:08,990 --> 00:24:11,952
I don't really have
the disposition for motherhood.

401
00:24:12,035 --> 00:24:14,538
If my child wasn't cool
or good-looking,

402
00:24:14,621 --> 00:24:15,914
there's no way I'd love it.

403
00:24:15,997 --> 00:24:17,415
Well, not me.

404
00:24:17,499 --> 00:24:18,875
I loved them all.

405
00:24:18,959 --> 00:24:21,503
It was Michael

406
00:24:21,586 --> 00:24:24,214
who made me realize

407
00:24:24,297 --> 00:24:26,508
that I was put on this earth

408
00:24:26,591 --> 00:24:29,761
to raise the monsters.

409
00:24:33,974 --> 00:24:35,725
<i>I never thought I would tire</i>

410
00:24:35,809 --> 00:24:37,811
<i>of the smell of roses.</i>

411
00:24:39,646 --> 00:24:42,691
<i>Roses had always been
my favorite flower,</i>

412
00:24:42,774 --> 00:24:46,319
<i>but soon they made me</i>

413
00:24:46,403 --> 00:24:48,405
<i>just want to retch.</i>

414
00:24:53,076 --> 00:24:57,789
<i>And of course then there was
that incident with the sitter.</i>

415
00:25:01,543 --> 00:25:03,545
<i>I was able to convince
the authorities</i>

416
00:25:03,628 --> 00:25:06,256
<i>that she had taken
her own life.</i>

417
00:25:06,339 --> 00:25:07,757
<i>(Michael giggles)</i>

418
00:25:07,841 --> 00:25:10,552
At least I didn't have
to bury that one.

419
00:25:10,635 --> 00:25:12,721
Um, up until that point,

420
00:25:12,804 --> 00:25:14,723
<i>I thought I was raising</i>

421
00:25:14,806 --> 00:25:18,435
<i>a garden variety serial killer,</i>

422
00:25:18,518 --> 00:25:21,938
<i>or possibly even a gifted one...</i>

423
00:25:22,022 --> 00:25:24,191
<i>you know, with its</i>

424
00:25:24,274 --> 00:25:26,151
<i>attendant challenges.</i>

425
00:25:26,234 --> 00:25:28,153
<i>But then came the day
when he was late</i>

426
00:25:28,236 --> 00:25:30,697
<i>getting up for school,</i>

427
00:25:30,780 --> 00:25:33,200
<i>so I went in to wake him.</i>

428
00:25:35,035 --> 00:25:37,954
<i>And there was a stranger
in his bed.</i>

429
00:25:39,706 --> 00:25:41,041
<i>Well, not a stranger,</i>

430
00:25:41,124 --> 00:25:42,959
<i>I mean, it was still my grandson.</i>

431
00:25:43,043 --> 00:25:47,547
<i>He'd aged a decade overnight.</i>

432
00:25:47,631 --> 00:25:49,883
Now, that was something

433
00:25:49,966 --> 00:25:52,969
far outside the natural realm.

434
00:25:55,847 --> 00:25:58,725
<i>It was almost as if he was</i>

435
00:25:58,808 --> 00:26:01,561
<i>in a hurry to get somewhere,</i>

436
00:26:01,645 --> 00:26:05,065
age-wise, know what I mean?

437
00:26:05,148 --> 00:26:07,609
<i>(Choking)</i>

438
00:26:09,778 --> 00:26:11,947
You don't tell me
what to do anymore.

439
00:26:21,873 --> 00:26:23,875
<i>(Gasping)</i>

440
00:26:29,547 --> 00:26:31,299
Grandma?

441
00:26:31,383 --> 00:26:34,135
<i>(Crying)</i> Oh.

442
00:26:40,267 --> 00:26:41,935
I'm-I'm sorry.

443
00:26:46,273 --> 00:26:48,608
Can I have a glass of water?

444
00:26:48,692 --> 00:26:50,777
<i>(Stammers)</i>

445
00:26:50,860 --> 00:26:53,780
M-M<i>... May</i> I?

446
00:26:53,863 --> 00:26:57,867
M... May I?

447
00:26:57,951 --> 00:27:02,747
Yes. Yes, you may.

448
00:27:02,831 --> 00:27:04,833
<i>(Crying)</i>

449
00:27:14,217 --> 00:27:16,219
<i>When you look at men
of significance,</i>

450
00:27:16,303 --> 00:27:20,473
<i>you know, like artists
or world leaders,</i>

451
00:27:20,557 --> 00:27:23,351
<i>inventors, they have all had</i>

452
00:27:23,435 --> 00:27:25,812
their particular peccadilloes

453
00:27:25,895 --> 00:27:27,647
on their road to the top,
haven't they?

454
00:27:27,731 --> 00:27:32,068
<i>But aging ten years
overnight...</i>

455
00:27:33,945 --> 00:27:36,531
...that called
for sacred intervention.

456
00:27:38,491 --> 00:27:40,577
<i>(Game device chiming)</i>

457
00:27:46,207 --> 00:27:50,211
<i>I had to accept
that once again,</i>

458
00:27:50,295 --> 00:27:54,299
<i>my days as a mother
were at an end.</i>

459
00:27:54,382 --> 00:28:00,180
I have been burdened
with heartbreak my whole life.

460
00:28:00,263 --> 00:28:04,059
Broken dreams, broken promises,
broken marriages.

461
00:28:04,142 --> 00:28:06,978
But this one...

462
00:28:11,066 --> 00:28:13,610
<i>(Laughs)</i>

463
00:28:13,693 --> 00:28:19,282
...this one shattered me
beyond recovery.

464
00:28:19,366 --> 00:28:21,701
<i>Michael had made me believe</i>

465
00:28:21,785 --> 00:28:27,332
<i>that my presence here
meant something.</i>

466
00:28:31,127 --> 00:28:33,254
That I mattered.

467
00:28:33,338 --> 00:28:35,173
<i>(Sniffles)</i>

468
00:28:35,256 --> 00:28:40,470
But I was just an invisible step
along the path.

469
00:28:41,721 --> 00:28:46,059
He was done with me.

470
00:28:46,142 --> 00:28:50,688
Honestly, I think that...

471
00:28:50,772 --> 00:28:55,110
if I had corrected his grammar
one more time,

472
00:28:55,193 --> 00:28:59,114
he would've just slit my throat.

473
00:28:59,197 --> 00:29:02,575
Like the help.

474
00:29:02,659 --> 00:29:04,411
I wasn't going to give him

475
00:29:04,494 --> 00:29:07,038
<i>or any man the satisfaction.</i>

476
00:29:07,122 --> 00:29:10,166
<i>I have always lived my life</i>

477
00:29:10,250 --> 00:29:13,461
<i>on my own terms.</i>

478
00:29:13,545 --> 00:29:18,174
<i>So I came here.</i>

479
00:29:18,258 --> 00:29:20,593
<i>A prison, yes.</i>

480
00:29:20,677 --> 00:29:24,556
<i>But one where I knew the rules,
and more importantly...</i>

481
00:29:24,639 --> 00:29:26,033
<i>("You're Gonna Miss Me"
by Connie Francis playing)</i>

482
00:29:26,057 --> 00:29:29,811
<i>...where I knew the company.</i>

484
00:29:39,737 --> 00:29:43,074
<i>♪ One kiss ♪</i>

485
00:29:43,158 --> 00:29:47,537
<i>♪ One little sigh ♪</i>

486
00:29:47,620 --> 00:29:51,666
<i>Bottle of whiskey
and a fenny chaser.</i>

487
00:29:51,749 --> 00:29:53,668
<i>(Laughs softly)</i>

488
00:29:53,751 --> 00:29:57,338
<i>Ooh, that's what I call
a bon voyage.</i>

489
00:29:57,422 --> 00:30:01,676
<i>♪ Someday, baby, someday, darling ♪</i>

490
00:30:02,802 --> 00:30:06,055
<i>♪ You're gonna miss me ♪</i>

491
00:30:06,139 --> 00:30:10,101
<i>♪ Hmm ♪</i>

492
00:30:10,185 --> 00:30:13,688
<i>♪ Long gone ♪</i>

493
00:30:13,771 --> 00:30:17,066
<i>♪ Is your caress ♪</i>

494
00:30:17,150 --> 00:30:19,527
<i>♪ And with it ♪</i>

495
00:30:19,611 --> 00:30:24,657
<i>♪ All of my happiness ♪</i>

496
00:30:24,741 --> 00:30:28,870
<i>♪ But someday, baby ♪</i>

497
00:30:28,953 --> 00:30:32,499
<i>♪ Someday, darling ♪</i>

498
00:30:32,582 --> 00:30:38,171
<i>♪ You're gonna miss me ♪</i>

499
00:30:38,254 --> 00:30:42,592
<i>♪ Oh, oh, oh ♪</i>

500
00:30:42,675 --> 00:30:44,052
<i>♪ Yes ♪</i>

501
00:30:44,135 --> 00:30:47,347
<i>I awoke to find myself</i>

502
00:30:47,430 --> 00:30:50,141
<i>surrounded
by my precious children.</i>

503
00:30:51,392 --> 00:30:53,937
<i>Well, minus my beloved Addie.</i>

504
00:30:54,020 --> 00:30:56,022
<i>God rest her soul.</i>

505
00:30:56,105 --> 00:30:58,191
<i>But the others were there.</i>

506
00:30:58,274 --> 00:31:00,735
<i>All of them.</i>

507
00:31:00,818 --> 00:31:04,989
<i>With me, forever.</i>

508
00:31:05,073 --> 00:31:08,409
<i>And that is the real reason</i>

509
00:31:08,493 --> 00:31:11,204
<i>I bound my soul to this place.</i>

510
00:31:11,287 --> 00:31:16,417
<i>Because, like I said earlier,</i>

511
00:31:16,501 --> 00:31:20,255
<i>I was born to be a mother.</i>

512
00:31:20,338 --> 00:31:24,592
<i>Why not die to be one, too?</i>

513
00:31:24,676 --> 00:31:28,596
As for my grandson...

514
00:31:28,680 --> 00:31:31,975
I never wanted to see him again.

515
00:31:36,688 --> 00:31:38,022
Well, there it is.

516
00:31:38,106 --> 00:31:39,691
<i>(Exhales)</i>

517
00:31:39,774 --> 00:31:41,651
The whole story.

518
00:31:41,734 --> 00:31:46,364
Was it everything
you dreamed of, witchypoos?

519
00:31:53,913 --> 00:31:55,832
GIRL: Mommy.

520
00:31:57,292 --> 00:31:58,543
Yes, my darling?

521
00:31:58,626 --> 00:31:59,961
It's almost tea time.

522
00:32:00,044 --> 00:32:03,756
Of course it is,
my little beauty queen.

523
00:32:03,840 --> 00:32:06,467
How foolish of me.
<i>(Laughs softly)</i>

524
00:32:08,428 --> 00:32:10,763
Well, now.

525
00:32:10,847 --> 00:32:13,141
You'll have to excuse me now.

526
00:32:13,224 --> 00:32:15,560
My family calls.

527
00:32:22,859 --> 00:32:24,902
Let's go.

528
00:32:38,041 --> 00:32:40,501
<i>(Moaning)</i>

529
00:32:45,506 --> 00:32:47,925
<i>(Crying)</i>

530
00:32:55,558 --> 00:32:58,144
You gonna be much longer, DILF?

531
00:32:58,227 --> 00:33:01,648
What the hell?
People don't knock anymore?

532
00:33:01,731 --> 00:33:04,317
We still need to talk to you
about Michael.

533
00:33:04,400 --> 00:33:06,569
BEHOLD: We're leaving
no stone unturned.

534
00:33:06,653 --> 00:33:08,571
I still have nothing
to say to you. Now get out.

535
00:33:08,655 --> 00:33:11,366
What if we were to fix it so you
didn't have to do that anymore?

536
00:33:13,743 --> 00:33:15,495
Stand at the window, crying,

537
00:33:15,578 --> 00:33:18,665
while you double-click
your mouse?

538
00:33:18,748 --> 00:33:20,833
You could do that?

539
00:33:20,917 --> 00:33:23,461
You can make the impulse stop?

540
00:33:25,755 --> 00:33:27,915
Actually, it's only the crying
part I can live without.

541
00:33:29,801 --> 00:33:35,390
<i>The day Constance died
was when I first saw my son.</i>

542
00:33:37,517 --> 00:33:39,519
Grandma?

543
00:33:42,230 --> 00:33:44,232
Grandma!

544
00:33:47,944 --> 00:33:49,946
Grandma?

545
00:33:56,577 --> 00:33:59,789
<i>(Crying)</i> No.

546
00:34:04,001 --> 00:34:07,588
No. Hey. Hey, wake up.

547
00:34:07,672 --> 00:34:09,924
Hey, wake up.

548
00:34:11,509 --> 00:34:13,219
I'm sorry.

549
00:34:13,302 --> 00:34:15,847
I'm so sorry.

550
00:34:15,930 --> 00:34:18,266
It's all my fault.

551
00:34:18,349 --> 00:34:20,727
Hey.

552
00:34:20,810 --> 00:34:21,936
Grandma.

553
00:34:22,019 --> 00:34:24,021
BEN: The spirits in this house

554
00:34:24,105 --> 00:34:28,234
can't be seen
unless they want to be seen.

555
00:34:28,317 --> 00:34:31,070
She doesn't want to see me?

556
00:34:31,154 --> 00:34:33,448
I'm sorry.

557
00:34:33,531 --> 00:34:36,242
Who are you?

558
00:34:36,325 --> 00:34:39,829
Someone who wants to be seen.

559
00:34:39,912 --> 00:34:41,914
Someone who wants to help.

560
00:34:44,208 --> 00:34:47,170
If you really want to change,
I think I can show you how.

561
00:34:47,253 --> 00:34:51,090
I'm a monster.

562
00:34:51,174 --> 00:34:53,092
Why would you want to help me?

563
00:34:53,176 --> 00:34:55,678
Because I can't help
but think of you as my son.

564
00:34:57,805 --> 00:35:00,892
Even though you're not, really.

565
00:35:00,975 --> 00:35:05,354
<i>And so we started talking,
doctor to patient,</i>

566
00:35:05,438 --> 00:35:06,856
<i>on that very day.</i>

567
00:35:09,025 --> 00:35:12,612
<i>He wanted to be good,
desperately.</i>

568
00:35:12,695 --> 00:35:16,991
<i>I could see in his eyes
how much he needed me.</i>

570
00:35:18,659 --> 00:35:20,828
<i>I wanted him to have
all the simple joys</i>

571
00:35:20,912 --> 00:35:23,790
<i>he never had without
a real father to show him how.</i>

572
00:35:23,873 --> 00:35:26,334
<i>♪ To somebody new ♪</i>

573
00:35:26,417 --> 00:35:30,213
<i>He was brilliant,
off the charts.</i>

574
00:35:30,296 --> 00:35:33,758
<i>His brain always seemed five
steps ahead of everyone else.</i>

575
00:35:36,385 --> 00:35:37,637
<i>♪ Although ♪</i>

576
00:35:37,720 --> 00:35:39,263
<i>The more time I spent with him,</i>

577
00:35:39,347 --> 00:35:41,766
<i>the more I began to feel
like a father to this boy.</i>

578
00:35:41,849 --> 00:35:43,392
<i>♪ You're a part of my heart ♪</i>

579
00:35:43,476 --> 00:35:45,102
<i>Everything in this house was dead.</i>

580
00:35:45,186 --> 00:35:47,021
<i>My wife,</i>

581
00:35:47,104 --> 00:35:48,898
<i>My baby was never going
to grow up.</i>

582
00:35:48,981 --> 00:35:52,777
<i>Violet was never going
to get married.</i>

583
00:35:52,860 --> 00:35:55,404
<i>But Michael was alive,</i>

584
00:35:55,488 --> 00:35:57,490
<i>the only light
to come out of all this.</i>

585
00:35:57,573 --> 00:35:58,866
Ow.

586
00:35:58,950 --> 00:36:01,494
<i>I wanted to give him everything.</i>

587
00:36:01,577 --> 00:36:05,248
<i>♪ It will seem once more just to ♪</i>

588
00:36:05,331 --> 00:36:07,011
What are you doing?
Stay away from my shit.

589
00:36:08,543 --> 00:36:10,419
- He was just exploring.
- He's fucked-up.

590
00:36:10,503 --> 00:36:12,255
You stay away from my shit,
you understand?

591
00:36:12,338 --> 00:36:15,299
I just want
to be like you, Dad.

592
00:36:17,677 --> 00:36:19,053
Who told you that?

593
00:36:19,136 --> 00:36:22,390
Other spirits.

594
00:36:22,473 --> 00:36:24,642
They whispered to me.

595
00:36:24,725 --> 00:36:26,769
You didn't spring
from my nutsack, got it?

596
00:36:28,187 --> 00:36:29,915
Not even I could create
something as monstrous,

597
00:36:29,939 --> 00:36:31,357
as evil, as you.

598
00:36:33,818 --> 00:36:36,529
You stay away from me.

599
00:36:42,994 --> 00:36:44,996
BEN:
<i>I could see him turning away.</i>

600
00:36:47,498 --> 00:36:49,959
<i>Turning to the dark side.</i>

601
00:36:52,336 --> 00:36:54,130
And it was about to get worse.

602
00:36:55,548 --> 00:36:59,468
<i>The darkness was always
on the edges.</i>

603
00:36:59,552 --> 00:37:01,762
<i>Encroaching.</i>

604
00:37:01,846 --> 00:37:05,266
<i>It's impossible to avoid
in this house.</i>

605
00:37:16,485 --> 00:37:18,195
What are you doing?

606
00:37:21,407 --> 00:37:24,201
Giving her a smile.

607
00:37:24,285 --> 00:37:28,164
The things you have
to do to be a star.

608
00:37:28,247 --> 00:37:29,957
BEN:
<i>I was losing him.</i>

609
00:37:37,965 --> 00:37:40,092
<i>And then the house sold.</i>

610
00:37:40,176 --> 00:37:42,178
<i>(Engine receding)</i>

611
00:37:44,263 --> 00:37:46,390
- Ooh...
- Hey.

612
00:37:46,474 --> 00:37:48,809
That's it, baby.

613
00:37:48,893 --> 00:37:50,519
- We did it.
- Okay.

614
00:37:50,603 --> 00:37:52,563
- Last one.
- Okay.

615
00:37:52,647 --> 00:37:54,941
All right, here we go.

616
00:37:55,024 --> 00:37:57,526
Ooh!

617
00:38:09,914 --> 00:38:11,832
- <i>(Knife slices)</i>
- <i>(Women screaming)</i>

618
00:38:15,503 --> 00:38:17,296
No, no, no, no!

619
00:38:37,400 --> 00:38:39,068
<i>(Panting)</i>

620
00:38:40,653 --> 00:38:43,072
Those were good people.

621
00:38:43,155 --> 00:38:44,824
They deserved a chance.

622
00:38:44,907 --> 00:38:47,076
They don't belong here.

623
00:38:47,159 --> 00:38:49,328
Because of what you did,
they'll be here forever.

624
00:38:51,455 --> 00:38:52,790
<i>(Whimpers)</i>

625
00:38:52,873 --> 00:38:54,667
GRACE: What's happening?

626
00:38:55,918 --> 00:38:58,129
I don't feel right.

627
00:38:58,212 --> 00:39:01,882
You didn't have to kill them.

628
00:39:01,966 --> 00:39:05,344
I know you.
This isn't who you are.

629
00:39:08,806 --> 00:39:10,599
<i>(Grace and Elizabeth screaming)</i>

630
00:39:18,107 --> 00:39:19,942
<i>(Grunts)</i>

631
00:39:31,412 --> 00:39:33,539
I never could have helped you.

632
00:39:35,207 --> 00:39:37,835
It was foolish to try.

633
00:39:51,849 --> 00:39:54,268
<i>Michael didn't just kill
those women.</i>

634
00:39:54,351 --> 00:39:58,731
He made them cease to exist.

635
00:39:58,814 --> 00:40:01,567
He murdered their bodies

636
00:40:01,650 --> 00:40:06,238
and then destroyed their souls.

637
00:40:06,322 --> 00:40:07,990
Fuck.

638
00:40:08,074 --> 00:40:11,327
So, basically, our new Supreme
is pretty much pure evil.

639
00:40:13,412 --> 00:40:14,538
We should go.

640
00:40:14,622 --> 00:40:16,207
Cordelia will know what to do.

641
00:40:16,290 --> 00:40:17,833
How to get rid of him.

642
00:40:17,917 --> 00:40:20,795
It won't be so easy.

643
00:40:26,133 --> 00:40:27,259
Vivien.

644
00:40:27,343 --> 00:40:29,095
Ben.

645
00:40:30,137 --> 00:40:32,681
Are we speaking again?

646
00:40:32,765 --> 00:40:35,226
I don't know yet.

647
00:40:35,309 --> 00:40:38,104
Every haunted house
has a cold spot,

648
00:40:38,187 --> 00:40:40,147
and I think we just found it.

649
00:40:40,231 --> 00:40:43,109
I never stopped loving you.

650
00:40:43,192 --> 00:40:46,112
I know.

651
00:40:46,195 --> 00:40:51,742
But I never stopped hating him.

652
00:40:51,826 --> 00:40:54,411
And I couldn't forgive you
for needing Michael.

653
00:40:57,039 --> 00:40:59,375
Although, just now,
I'm starting to realize

654
00:40:59,458 --> 00:41:01,127
maybe you never had a choice.

655
00:41:01,210 --> 00:41:02,419
<i>(Baby crying)</i>

656
00:41:04,964 --> 00:41:06,924
Your son needs you, Ben.

657
00:41:07,007 --> 00:41:09,844
He needs his father.

658
00:41:19,979 --> 00:41:21,981
<i>(Baby continues crying)</i>

659
00:41:25,526 --> 00:41:29,113
What you're dealing with here
is not just evil.

660
00:41:29,196 --> 00:41:33,826
Michael is not just a bad witch
for you to exterminate.

661
00:41:33,909 --> 00:41:36,412
What is that supposed to mean?

662
00:41:36,495 --> 00:41:41,667
"Then I saw a beast
with ten horns and seven heads

663
00:41:41,750 --> 00:41:44,795
"rising out of the sea

664
00:41:44,879 --> 00:41:48,632
and all who dwell on the Earth
will worship Him."

665
00:41:56,348 --> 00:41:59,852
Nothing about Michael
is natural to me,

666
00:41:59,935 --> 00:42:03,564
not his birth,
not his appearance.

667
00:42:03,647 --> 00:42:08,694
I kept away from him at first
because it was painful.

668
00:42:08,777 --> 00:42:11,447
And then strange things
started to happen.

669
00:42:11,530 --> 00:42:16,577
<i>A murder of crows would
encircle the house every day.</i>

670
00:42:20,122 --> 00:42:23,375
<i>Inside it was sweltering hot.</i>

671
00:42:30,382 --> 00:42:32,801
<i>And then they came.</i>

672
00:42:40,184 --> 00:42:43,187
<i>(Doorbell rings)</i>

673
00:42:57,409 --> 00:43:01,163
"And the son became black
as sackcloth with hair,

674
00:43:01,247 --> 00:43:05,334
"and the whole moon
became as blood...

675
00:43:05,417 --> 00:43:09,421
"and the stars fell
from the Heaven to the Earth,

676
00:43:09,505 --> 00:43:13,008
for the great day of wrath
is come."

677
00:43:16,345 --> 00:43:19,390
<i>(Gasps)</i>
I am in the presence of my Lord.

678
00:43:23,102 --> 00:43:25,479
Who are you?

679
00:43:25,562 --> 00:43:31,235
I am Anton LaVey, Black Pope
of the Church of Satan,

680
00:43:31,318 --> 00:43:34,071
and these are my cardinals.

681
00:43:34,154 --> 00:43:37,950
I faked my death
to prepare for this day.

682
00:43:40,744 --> 00:43:43,914
I have no idea
what you're talking about.

683
00:43:43,998 --> 00:43:46,709
What's going on here?

684
00:43:46,792 --> 00:43:49,503
We followed a dark star
from the west.

685
00:43:49,586 --> 00:43:52,131
The signs are impossible
to miss:

686
00:43:52,214 --> 00:43:54,591
the temperature in this house,

687
00:43:54,675 --> 00:43:57,594
a home built
over the portal to Hell,

688
00:43:57,678 --> 00:44:01,056
and the crows worshipping
from above.

689
00:44:01,140 --> 00:44:02,599
The omens are complete.

690
00:44:02,683 --> 00:44:04,768
You're the chosen one.

691
00:44:04,852 --> 00:44:08,647
The time has come to remove
the scales from your eyes,

692
00:44:08,731 --> 00:44:11,275
to show you your true power.

693
00:44:11,358 --> 00:44:13,861
VIVIEN:
<i>Something changed in Michael.</i>

694
00:44:13,944 --> 00:44:17,239
It was like they opened a door

695
00:44:17,323 --> 00:44:19,992
and they showed him
his true path.

696
00:44:20,075 --> 00:44:21,785
Why didn't you stop them?

697
00:44:21,869 --> 00:44:23,829
I think I thought it was a joke.

698
00:44:23,912 --> 00:44:27,416
I mean, they were lost souls
following a con man

699
00:44:27,499 --> 00:44:29,543
from some pathetic circus.

700
00:44:29,626 --> 00:44:31,253
That's what it seemed like to me.

701
00:44:31,337 --> 00:44:33,756
That is, until the Black Mass.

702
00:44:54,193 --> 00:44:57,654
Oh, dear child,
you must be freezing.

703
00:44:57,738 --> 00:44:59,531
Hop in. I'll give you a ride.

704
00:44:59,615 --> 00:45:02,034
Thank you.

705
00:45:04,787 --> 00:45:07,122
<i>("(Don't Fear) The Reaper"
by Blue Oyster Cult playing)</i>

706
00:45:07,206 --> 00:45:09,249
You're a lifesaver.

707
00:45:13,128 --> 00:45:15,381
I'm just a couple miles
up Riverside.

708
00:45:15,464 --> 00:45:17,466
<i>♪ They're gone ♪</i>

709
00:45:19,093 --> 00:45:21,470
<i>♪ Seasons don't fear the reaper ♪</i>

710
00:45:25,099 --> 00:45:26,350
<i>♪ La, la, la, la, la ♪</i>

711
00:45:26,433 --> 00:45:29,019
You know something, I...

712
00:45:29,103 --> 00:45:30,312
I think I'd rather walk.

713
00:45:31,814 --> 00:45:34,566
It's not going to be possible.

714
00:45:37,444 --> 00:45:38,779
<i>(Whimpers)</i>

715
00:45:38,862 --> 00:45:41,448
But it's such a lovely night.

716
00:45:41,532 --> 00:45:42,908
Isn't it?

717
00:45:42,991 --> 00:45:44,910
For what?

718
00:45:44,993 --> 00:45:47,162
Murder.

719
00:45:59,174 --> 00:46:01,093
<i>(Moaning)</i>

720
00:46:05,973 --> 00:46:08,684
<i>(Door creaks open)</i>

721
00:46:08,767 --> 00:46:11,562
<i>Footfalls approaching)</i>

722
00:46:12,563 --> 00:46:14,565
<i>(Gasping)</i>

723
00:46:29,204 --> 00:46:32,958
<i>(Chanting in foreign language)</i>

724
00:46:51,685 --> 00:46:53,562
For you, Michael.

725
00:46:53,645 --> 00:46:56,982
It's all for you.

726
00:46:57,065 --> 00:46:59,026
Hail Satan!

727
00:46:59,109 --> 00:47:00,527
<i>(Shouts)</i>

728
00:47:03,530 --> 00:47:07,451
<i>(Screaming)</i>

729
00:47:23,884 --> 00:47:26,887
LaVEY: Oh! Oh!

730
00:47:32,726 --> 00:47:34,311
Oh!

732
00:48:10,931 --> 00:48:14,309
<i>(Carl Orff's "O Fortuna" playing)</i>

733
00:48:21,608 --> 00:48:24,695
<i>Ave Satanas.</i>

735
00:48:44,798 --> 00:48:48,010
Father.

736
00:48:48,093 --> 00:48:50,679
I am with you now.

737
00:48:57,227 --> 00:49:00,105
VIVIEN: <i>That night
was a terrible storm.</i>

738
00:49:00,188 --> 00:49:04,151
<i>Hail as big as rocks,</i>

739
00:49:04,234 --> 00:49:06,278
<i>rain of blood.</i>

740
00:49:06,361 --> 00:49:10,824
<i>It was then that I made
the decision to kill him.</i>

742
00:49:54,034 --> 00:49:57,204
<i>(Vivien screams)</i>

743
00:49:58,830 --> 00:50:00,791
Tate saved me.

744
00:50:00,874 --> 00:50:05,170
And after we put the fire out,
Michael was gone.

745
00:50:05,253 --> 00:50:06,713
I don't know where he went.

746
00:50:06,797 --> 00:50:10,258
I don't know who raised him
after he left.

747
00:50:10,342 --> 00:50:14,179
The only thing I know is, Ben
is not his father, nor is Tate.

748
00:50:14,262 --> 00:50:18,183
He was born from the evil
of this house.

749
00:50:18,266 --> 00:50:23,146
The source of darkness
is his true father,

750
00:50:23,230 --> 00:50:26,608
and he is here
to destroy the world.

751
00:50:26,692 --> 00:50:27,859
BEHOLD: <i>Madison.</i>

752
00:50:27,943 --> 00:50:29,986
Madison.

753
00:50:30,070 --> 00:50:31,863
Look, I know it sucks

754
00:50:31,947 --> 00:50:33,299
that the guy you put
your hopes into

755
00:50:33,323 --> 00:50:35,075
turned out to be the Antichrist,

756
00:50:35,158 --> 00:50:37,011
but you are not stopping me
from telling the council.

757
00:50:37,035 --> 00:50:38,370
I wasn't gonna stop you.

758
00:50:40,122 --> 00:50:42,122
I never would have fought
for Michael to be Supreme

759
00:50:42,165 --> 00:50:45,335
if I had any idea
about who he truly is.

760
00:50:45,419 --> 00:50:49,131
We just wanted a leader.

761
00:50:49,214 --> 00:50:51,883
But he is clearly not that.

762
00:50:51,967 --> 00:50:54,845
What if we can't stop him?

763
00:50:54,928 --> 00:50:56,388
What happens then?

764
00:50:58,390 --> 00:50:59,725
I don't know.

765
00:51:01,727 --> 00:51:04,146
<i>(Soft crying)</i>

766
00:51:10,694 --> 00:51:14,156
<i>(Crying)</i>

767
00:51:14,239 --> 00:51:16,867
Give me a second.

768
00:51:30,881 --> 00:51:33,383
If you want to ask me about
Michael, I can't help you.

769
00:51:33,467 --> 00:51:37,095
I stayed clear of him.

770
00:51:37,179 --> 00:51:40,223
Probably a good call.

771
00:51:40,307 --> 00:51:43,435
I think we got enough
on him anyway.

772
00:51:43,518 --> 00:51:44,853
Then what do you want?

773
00:51:44,936 --> 00:51:47,272
Seems like you're having
a hard time.

774
00:51:47,355 --> 00:51:50,525
You and that Tate guy have
a real angsty thing going on.

775
00:51:50,609 --> 00:51:52,027
We don't have anything.

776
00:51:53,570 --> 00:51:55,906
We can't.

777
00:51:55,989 --> 00:51:58,116
He's a monster.

778
00:51:58,200 --> 00:51:59,826
He didn't seem
like a monster to me.

779
00:51:59,910 --> 00:52:01,787
You don't know him.

780
00:52:01,870 --> 00:52:04,372
You can't imagine what it's like

781
00:52:04,456 --> 00:52:06,374
to know all of the horrible
things he's done.

782
00:52:06,458 --> 00:52:09,419
And still be in love with him?

783
00:52:10,629 --> 00:52:15,133
It's torture... every day.

784
00:52:15,217 --> 00:52:18,595
I've done some bad things I'm
not exactly proud of in my life

785
00:52:18,678 --> 00:52:21,681
and my second life.

786
00:52:21,765 --> 00:52:23,475
But those were my choices.

787
00:52:23,558 --> 00:52:27,562
I think what happened to Tate
was different.

788
00:52:27,646 --> 00:52:31,441
He wasn't the real evil here.

789
00:52:31,525 --> 00:52:32,859
What does that even mean?

790
00:52:32,943 --> 00:52:36,947
It's like this house
used him as a vessel

791
00:52:37,030 --> 00:52:39,616
to create something
way, way worse.

792
00:52:39,699 --> 00:52:44,246
My guess... any evil inside Tate
left with Michael.

793
00:52:48,458 --> 00:52:51,002
It would be nice if that were true.

794
00:52:51,086 --> 00:52:53,672
Maybe you just need to see
the truth for yourself.

796
00:53:25,704 --> 00:53:27,455
Tate?

797
00:53:37,215 --> 00:53:39,175
You saved my mom.

798
00:53:40,427 --> 00:53:43,305
I'm so sorry for everything. I...

799
00:53:43,388 --> 00:53:45,640
I know.

800
00:53:47,851 --> 00:53:50,478
<i>("Spirits in the Material World"
by The Police playing)</i>

801
00:53:56,109 --> 00:54:00,113
<i>♪ There is no political solution ♪</i>

802
00:54:02,782 --> 00:54:05,660
<i>♪ To our troubled evolution ♪</i>

803
00:54:05,744 --> 00:54:08,455
You're really nothing
but a softie, aren't you?

804
00:54:08,538 --> 00:54:10,624
Whatever.

805
00:54:10,707 --> 00:54:12,310
I just thought I'd help
two ghosts get laid.

806
00:54:12,334 --> 00:54:14,878
At least someone's gonna get
a happy ever after.

807
00:54:14,961 --> 00:54:17,047
There's not gonna be
an ever after for anyone

808
00:54:17,130 --> 00:54:18,650
if we don't find a way
to stop Michael.

809
00:54:21,801 --> 00:54:26,598
<i>♪ We are spirits in the material world ♪</i>

810
